% ============================================================================
% synonyms.query.adj — a worked recall over the word-synonyms library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is a synonym of
% happy?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `synonym`
% rows and returns the synonym + the table's source/locator/trust. A word the
% table does not carry abstains honestly — the engine never invents a synonym.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli synonyms.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "synonyms.adj"

? synonym(happy, $Word)        % expect cheerful
? synonym(quick, $Word)        % expect fast
? synonym(purple, $Word)       % expect abstain — no synonym is shipped for purple
